  "interpretation": "<table>\n<thead data-start=\"238\" data-end=\"569\">\n<tr data-start=\"238\" data-end=\"569\">\n<th data-start=\"238\" data-end=\"264\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Parameter</th>\n<th data-start=\"264\" data-end=\"419\" data-col-size=\"lg\">Description</th>\n<th data-start=\"419\" data-end=\"439\" data-col-size=\"md\">Units</th>\n<th data-start=\"439\" data-end=\"569\" data-col-size=\"lg\">Reference Range / Normal Finding</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n</table>\n<table>\n<tbody>\n<tr data-start=\"899\" data-end=\"1253\">\n<td data-start=\"899\" data-end=\"925\" data-col-size=\"sm\">5q Deletion (del5q)</td>\n<td data-col-size=\"lg\" data-start=\"925\" data-end=\"1086\">Deletion (loss) of part of the long arm of chromosome 5, often involving the EGR1 gene. This is a common abnormality in MDS and may indicate better prognosis.</td>\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"1086\" data-end=\"1134\">Percentage of cells with deletion (usually %)</td>\n<td data-col-size=\"lg\" data-start=\"1134\" data-end=\"1253\">Normal: 0&ndash;5% cells show deletion (considered background/no deletion) <br>Abnormal: &gt;5% cells show deletion</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<table>\n<tbody>\n<tr data-start=\"1254\" data-end=\"1563\">\n<td data-start=\"1254\" data-end=\"1290\" data-col-size=\"sm\">7q Deletion / Monosomy 7 (-7)</td>\n<td data-col-size=\"lg\" data-start=\"1290\" data-end=\"1444\">Deletion of part of chromosome 7 (7q) or loss of the entire chromosome 7. Seen in high-risk MDS and poor prognosis.</td>\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"1444\" data-end=\"1470\">Percentage of cells (%)</td>\n<td data-col-size=\"lg\" data-start=\"1470\" data-end=\"1563\">Normal: 0&ndash;5% cells show deletion/loss <br>Abnormal: &gt;5% cells show deletion/loss</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<table style=\"width: 99.9731%;\">\n<tbody>\n<tr data-start=\"1564\" data-end=\"1850\">\n<td style=\"width: 13.2154%;\" data-start=\"1564\" data-end=\"1589\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Trisomy 8 (+8)</td>\n<td data-col-size=\"lg\" data-start=\"1589\" data-end=\"1743\">Extra copy of chromosome 8, common in MDS.</td>\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"1743\" data-end=\"1769\">Percentage of cells (%)</td>\n<td style=\"width: 28.8727%;\" data-col-size=\"lg\" data-start=\"1769\" data-end=\"1850\">Normal: 0&ndash;5% cells show trisomy <br>Abnormal: &gt;5% cells show trisomy</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<table>\n<tbody>\n<tr data-start=\"1851\" data-end=\"2142\">\n<td data-start=\"1851\" data-end=\"1879\" data-col-size=\"sm\">20q Deletion (del20q)</td>\n<td data-col-size=\"lg\" data-start=\"1879\" data-end=\"2033\">Deletion in part of chromosome 20, often associated with low-risk MDS.</td>\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"2033\" data-end=\"2059\">Percentage of cells (%)</td>\n<td data-col-size=\"lg\" data-start=\"2059\" data-end=\"2142\">Normal: 0&ndash;5% cells with deletion <br>Abnormal: &gt;5% cells with deletion</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<table style=\"width: 99.9731%;\">\n<tbody>\n<tr data-start=\"2143\" data-end=\"2446\">\n<td style=\"width: 8.76237%;\" data-start=\"2143\" data-end=\"2168\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Loss of Y (-Y)</td>\n<td data-col-size=\"lg\" data-start=\"2168\" data-end=\"2323\">Loss of the Y chromosome, typically found in older males and usually not clinically significant in MDS.</td>\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"2323\" data-end=\"2349\">Percentage of cells (%)</td>\n<td style=\"width: 27.149%;\" data-col-size=\"lg\" data-start=\"2349\" data-end=\"2446\">Normal: 0&ndash;5% cells with loss <br>Abnormal: &gt;5% cells with loss (usually age-related)</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>",
